# Accepted vulnerability findings: scripts/scan.sh hands this file to Trivy, which then leaves these IDs out of the
# report, the SARIF upload and the policy check. Use it only for a fixable CRITICAL in our own layers that can't be
# fixed right away (the policy: docs/dev/yolks.md, "Vulnerability scans"). Every entry needs a comment line right
# above it saying why, and an expiry date, after which Trivy reports the finding again:
#
#   # proton: GE-Proton's bundled curl, fixed in the next GE release (issue #123)
#   CVE-2026-12345 exp:2026-12-31
#
# test/check-workflows.sh fails an entry without both.

# python_*: pip's vendored urllib3 2.7.0 (pip/_vendor); pip 26.2.2, the newest on 2026-10-25, still ships it (fix: 2.8.0)
CVE-2026-97689 exp:2027-01-31
# python_*: the same vendored urllib3 2.7.0 in pip 26.2.2, a second issue fixed in 2.8.0
CVE-2026-97687 exp:2027-01-31
# python_*: pip 26.2.2's vendored msgpack 1.1.2 (fix: 1.2.1, not vendored by any pip release yet)
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 exp:2027-01-31
# python_*: pip 26.2.2's vendored setuptools 70.3.0 (pkg_resources; fix: 78.1.1, not vendored by any pip release yet)
CVE-2025-47273 exp:2027-01-31
# nodejs_*: undici 6.29.0 inside npm 11.21.1 (and 12.2.1, the newest on 2026-10-25); fixed in 6.29.1, which no npm
# release bundles yet. Drop it and raise NPM_VERSION when one does.
CVE-2026-109869 exp:2027-01-31
